<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 30,335,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 30,335,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 01/29/97    01/22/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 30,335,000  29,697,000    26,801,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	 181,490     144,984	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	34,948,000  34,948,000    33,981,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,140,728  35,140,728	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA.  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   01/29/97    01/22/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   5,460,000   5,116,000     4,888,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    5,089,000   5,034,000     4,358,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  5,054,000   4,922,000     4,922,000</p>
<p> South Central    3,216,000   3,223,000     2,362,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  4,194,000   4,135,000     3,503,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,315,000   5,188,000     4,862,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  2,007,000   2,077,000     1,906,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	30,335,000  29,697,000    26,801,000</p>
